.TH CONTEXTPACK 1 "2026-10-24" "cools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
contextpack \- pack text files into a bounded context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B contextpack
[\fIDIRECTORY\fR] (\fB--budget\fR \fIBYTES\fR | \fB--tokens\fR \fIN\fR) [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Select text files (smallest first) and print their contents until the budget is reached.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --budget N
Maximum bytes of output.
.TP
.B --tokens N
Maximum tokens (approximated as bytes=N*4).
.TP
.B --ext LIST
Comma-separated extensions.
.TP
.B --max-file N
Skip files larger than N bytes.
.TP
.B --all
Include non-text files.
.SH OUTPUT
File sections: ===== PATH ===== followed by contents.
.SH EXAMPLES
contextpack . --tokens 2000 --ext c,h
.SH SEE ALSO
bigfiles(1), changed(1), fileinfo(1)
